# Two-Machine Sync Protocol

This repo is worked on **two machines** (MacBook Air `~/Smash repair Engine/` and
Mac Studio `/Volumes/Goldman Global/businesses/claimdesk247/`), kept in sync via git.
Because the other machine may have committed work you haven't seen, **you must
sync with origin before starting any new commit work** — even if the user forgets
to ask. This prevents building on stale code and creating avoidable conflicts.

## Before ANY commit work (mandatory, even if the user doesn't ask)

Run `./scripts/sync-from-origin.sh` (or the equivalent steps). It:

1. Verifies the active `gh` user is `CTO-goldmanglobal` (guards against the
   3-business-account mix-up). If wrong, stop and tell the user — do NOT switch
   accounts autonomously.
2. `git fetch origin` to see remote state.
3. Reports whether local is behind / ahead / diverged.
4. If behind: stashes any local noise (e.g. `.DS_Store`), pulls with `--rebase`,
   syncs the submodule, drops the stash.
5. Reports the new HEAD and a one-line summary of what landed.

After sync, run the health check:
```bash
cd stage-3 && PYTHONPATH=. python3 tests/run_acceptance.py     # 50/50 + injury-ext
cd ../stage-2.5 && PYTHONPATH=. python3 tests/run_acceptance.py # 19/19
cd .. && python3 stage-4/scripts/sign_rule_trees.py --verify   # all trees live
```

## When to sync

- **Before** any commit work (always — even mid-session if a while has passed).
- **After** finishing work on one machine, before switching to the other
  (commit + push).

## Rules

- Use `git pull --rebase` (never merge commits) — keeps history linear.
- If the pull would conflict (local diverged from origin), STOP and show the
  user the divergence before resolving. Do not force-push, do not auto-resolve.
- Never push with the wrong `gh` account. If `gh auth status` ≠ CTO-goldmanglobal,
  stop and ask the user to switch.
- The `.DS_Store` file is tracked-but-ignored noise — if it blocks a pull,
  stash it (`git stash push -- .DS_Store`), pull, then drop the stash.

## Commit co-authoring

If a commit is made during a Paperclip agent heartbeat, append:
`Co-Authored-By: Paperclip <noreply@paperclip.ing>`. Manual/at-keyboard commits
do not need this trailer.
